sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API (api/routes/var.py)
    participant P as Postgres (var_jobs)
    participant B as Broker (SQS FIFO or Redis)
    participant W as Worker (tasks/var_task.py)
    participant E as engine/montecarlo.py
    participant S as S3
    participant R as Redis (result backend, job-done channel)

    C->>A: POST /api/v1/var/compute with Bearer credential
    Note over A: get_current_user, enforce_compute_rate_limit, cache_check
    Note over A: 403 if n_simulations is above the tier cap
    A->>P: INSERT var_jobs row, status pending
    A->>B: compute_var_task.apply_async with task_id
    A-->>C: 202 JobResponse with task_id
    B->>W: deliver message
    W->>E: run_monte_carlo_var
    E-->>W: var_pct, cvar_pct, loss_dist and more
    opt n_simulations above s3_result_offload_threshold
        W->>S: write_result_to_s3, loss_dist emptied
    end
    W->>P: UPDATE var_jobs to success or failure
    W->>R: publish on pyvar:var-job-done channel
    W-->>R: Celery stores the task result
    C->>A: GET /api/v1/var/result/task_id
    A->>R: read state and result from the Celery backend
    A-->>C: JobResultResponse with status and result
